<script lang="ts">
 import {MODEL_LABELS} from '@lib/ai/model';
 import {ArrowUpRight,ChevronDown,ShieldCheck} from 'lucide-svelte';
 import CategorySearch from '@lib/components/CategorySearch.svelte';
 import PublicNav from '@lib/components/PublicNav.svelte';
 import PublicFooter from '@lib/components/PublicFooter.svelte';
 let query=$state(''),expanded=$state(false);
 const aliases:Record<string,string[]>={glasses:['spectacles','sunglasses','eyeglasses'],lamp:['lamp','spotlight'],phone:['phone'],perfume:['perfume']};
 let filtered=$derived.by(()=>{const q=query.trim().toLowerCase(),terms=aliases[q]||[q];return MODEL_LABELS.filter(label=>!q||terms.some(term=>label.toLowerCase().includes(term))).sort((a,b)=>Number(b.toLowerCase().startsWith(q))-Number(a.toLowerCase().startsWith(q))||a.localeCompare(b,'en'));});
 let visible=$derived(expanded?filtered:filtered.slice(0,36));
</script>

<svelte:head><meta name="description" content="Get to know Visionary AI: everyday object detection, supported categories, its limits, and how your photos stay private."/></svelte:head>
<div id="top" class="landing studio-landing about-page">
 <PublicNav/>
 <main class="about-main">
  <header class="about-intro"><h1>About Visionary.</h1><p>A little more understanding of the things around you. Use your camera or a photo to explore objects, their shapes, and the discoveries you want to keep.</p></header>
  <nav class="about-index" aria-label="On this page"><a href="#model">How it works</a><a href="#categories">Supported categories</a><a href="#privacy">Privacy <ShieldCheck size={16}/></a></nav>

  <section id="model" class="about-section"><div><h2>A closer look,<br/>on your device.</h2></div><div class="about-body"><p>Visionary finds objects in camera views and photos, adds labels, and outlines their shapes. Try it without an account, or sign in to save snapshots and revisit them in your history.</p><p>Analysis runs in your browser. Your camera keeps playing while the model works on separate frames, so labels may follow a moving object with a short delay. Saving a snapshot keeps the analyzed image and its matching results together.</p><h3>What to expect</h3><p>The model compares objects with {MODEL_LABELS.length.toLocaleString()} category names, including furniture, clothing, electronics, food, and animals. It can miss small, blurry, covered, or unfamiliar objects. A supported category is not a guarantee of a correct result.</p><p>Lowering the confidence threshold shows more possible objects; raising it filters out weaker detections. The score describes the proposed object region, so it does not guarantee that the final name is correct. A question mark means similar labels were close matches.</p><details><summary>Model details & licenses <ChevronDown size={18}/></summary><div class="technical-copy"><p>YOLOE-26s proposes object regions and instance segmentation. MobileCLIP2-S0 compares each region with the category names. Both models run locally, using WebGPU when available and WebAssembly otherwise.</p><p>Each scan verifies up to 20 proposed objects. Counts describe the latest analyzed frame, not unique objects across time. No tracking or identification is used. A label match is cosine similarity, not a probability.</p><p>The first analysis downloads about 90 MB of model weights plus label embeddings, then caches verified files when browser storage is available. Performance varies by device. Model assets are bundled with the app; runtime binaries load from jsDelivr.</p><p>YOLOE weights and Ultralytics use AGPL-3.0, with enterprise licensing available. MobileCLIP source and weights use Apple's respective source and model licenses. Model exports, integrity hashes, vocabulary, preprocessing, and validation are documented in the repository's ml directory.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://docs.ultralytics.com/models/yoloe/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">YOLOE documentation <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/apple-aiml-research/ml-mobileclip" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Apple MobileCLIP and licenses <ArrowUpRight size={15}/></a></div></details></div></section>

  <section id="categories" class="about-section"><div><h2>Find a familiar object.</h2><p>Explore the supported category names.</p></div><div class="about-body"><CategorySearch bind:query matches={filtered}/><p id="category-help" class="category-help">Choose a suggestion or search for an everyday object.</p><p class="category-count" aria-live="polite">{filtered.length.toLocaleString()} matching categories</p><div class="category-list">{#each visible as label}<span>{label}</span>{:else}<p>No matching category. Try another name; the model does not cover every possible object.</p>{/each}</div>{#if filtered.length>36}<button class="category-expand text-link" onclick={()=>expanded=!expanded}>{expanded?'Show fewer categories':`Show all ${filtered.length.toLocaleString()} categories`} <ChevronDown size={16}/></button>{/if}</div></section>

  <section id="privacy" class="about-section"><div><ShieldCheck size={27} class="privacy-icon"/><h2>Your photos.<br/>Your choice.</h2></div><div class="about-body"><h3>While you explore</h3><p>Camera frames and photos stay on your device during analysis. There is no paid AI API or server-side inference.</p><h3>When you save</h3><p>Only snapshots you choose to save are uploaded to private storage and linked to your account, along with their detection results. Access to saved images requires your account's permission and uses temporary image links.</p><h3>When you delete</h3><p>Deleting a snapshot removes it from your account history. If deleting the stored image fails, the app queues the deletion for another attempt.</p><details><summary>Account & storage details <ChevronDown size={18}/></summary><div class="technical-copy"><p>Compressed snapshots are stored in private Cloudinary storage; account records and predictions are stored in Neon PostgreSQL. Passwords use Argon2id. Sessions use HttpOnly cookies, short-lived JWTs, rotating refresh sessions, revocation, and CSRF protection. Client-generated predictions remain unverified server-side.</p></div></details></div></section>
 </main>
 <PublicFooter/>
</div>

